.TH TAEMA 1 "2026-10-29" "taema 0.8.0" "Tæma Manual"
.SH NAME
taema \- dependency-aware, self-managing cgroup v2 process scopes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B taema
.RI [GLOBAL] " COMMAND " [ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Tæma adopts processes into cgroup scopes, learns which leftovers are safe to
stop, and stops them under pair authority. A per-user daemon
.RB ( taema\ daemon )
owns lifecycle passes; the CLI reads state and sends requests over a Unix
socket.
.PP
Lifecycle modes, weakest first:
.BR observe ,
.BR adopt ,
.BR enforce ,
.BR auto .
.BI "taema mode " MODE
switches the running daemon without sudo.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Scopes and launching
.TP
.B taema run [--bind] [--owner PID] [--join] NAME CMD...
Run CMD inside scope-NAME, stopping the scope when the owner exits.
.TP
.B taema launch [--app NAME] [--unit UNIT] [--bind] -- CMD...
Reserve an app scope, attach, register provenance, and exec CMD.
.TP
.B taema kill NAME
Stop a scope; shared members are moved aside, not killed.
.TP
.B taema ls
List scopes.
.TP
.B taema top
Live process table sorted by CPU, memory, then PID.
.TP
.B taema tree
Process trees grouped under scope headers.
.SS Inspecting and teaching
.TP
.B taema status
Show daemon and policy status.
.TP
.B taema explain [TARGET]
Explain a process, scope, app, pair, or latest decision.
.B why
is an alias.
.TP
.B taema review [--interactive]
List pending reviews or answer them interactively.
.TP
.B taema answer ID CHOICE
Answer a review with stop, keep, standalone, or never.
.TP
.B taema teach OWNER SURVIVOR CHOICE
Record an explicit pair answer without waiting for a review.
.TP
.B taema learn show|apps|pairs|signatures
Inspect learned state.
.TP
.B taema history TARGET
Show the timeline of one app or scope.
.TP
.B taema recent
List the latest automatic actions.
.TP
.B taema report --day|--week|--month
Summarize cleanup activity.
.TP
.B taema events [--since SEQ] [--follow]
Query or follow the event log.
.TP
.B taema dash
Curses dashboard; --once prints one snapshot.
.TP
.B taema prompt
Print the cached prompt summary without contacting the daemon.
.TP
.B taema bar --format waybar|i3bar|json|plain [--follow]
Stream bar state, one line per state change.
.SS Acting and overruling
.TP
.B taema keep TARGET
Keep an executable or owner/survivor pair.
.TP
.B taema do-not-kill TARGET
Veto a target or the latest automatic stop.
.TP
.B taema forget TARGET
Forget an executable or veto.
.TP
.B taema undo [ID]
Reverse a retained automatic action.
.TP
.B taema restore ID
Relaunch a stopped root by decision id.
.TP
.B taema mute APP
Mute an app's notifications.
.TP
.B taema hold [TARGET]
Pause actions without changing mode.
.TP
.B taema resume [TARGET]
Resume actions.
.TP
.B taema snooze DURATION|until TIME
Hold all actions for a duration or until a local time.
.TP
.B taema freeze SCOPE
Manually freeze a safe leftover scope.
.TP
.B taema thaw [SCOPE|--all]
Thaw managed scopes.
.TP
.B taema gc [--dry-run] [--memory]
Show or collect idle scopes.
.TP
.B taema adopt
Adopt eligible processes into scopes.
.SS Configuration and units
.TP
.B taema mode MODE
Switch lifecycle mode without restarting the daemon.
.TP
.B taema profile NAME
Select a configuration profile or return to automatic selection.
.TP
.B taema config
Show or edit layered configuration.
.TP
.B taema reload
Reload configuration and units in the daemon.
.TP
.B taema unit new|draft|test|dry-run|lint
Unit authoring tools.
.SS Desktop and session
.TP
.B taema desktop wrap|unwrap|list
Wrap launcher entries with taema launch.
.TP
.B taema agent
Relay this session's desktop facts to the daemon.
.TP
.B taema watch
Print live changes as plain lines.
.SS Maintenance
.TP
.B taema doctor
Check system support and report setup problems.
.TP
.B taema backup [--to FILE]
Write a tarball with the database, user config, and user units.
.TP
.B taema restore-backup FILE
Restore state, config, and units from a backup tarball.
.TP
.B taema reset --learning|--vetoes|--history|--all
Clear state after a backup.
.TP
.B taema memory [top|pressure|budget|watch|reclaim]
Host and per-scope memory accounting.
.TP
.B taema daemon
Run the per-user daemon.
.SH OPTIONS
Global options accepted before or after the command:
.BR --json ,
.BR --jsonl ,
.BR --plain ,
.BR --wide ,
.BR --no-color ,
.BR --quiet ,
.BR --yes ,
.BR --socket " PATH" ,
.BR --config " PATH" ,
.BR --verbose .
Read commands emit schema-tagged JSON with
.BR --json .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/taema/taema.toml
System configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/taema/taema.toml
User configuration; drop-ins live in
.IR taema.d .
.TP
.I /etc/taema/units, ~/.config/taema/units
Unit files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/applications
User desktop entry overrides written by
.BR "taema desktop wrap" .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B taema run editor code .
Start the editor inside scope-editor.
.TP
.B taema launch --app firefox -- firefox
Start firefox inside its own reserved app scope.
.TP
.B taema why scope-firefox
Explain what tæma would do to the scope and why.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR taema.toml (5),
.BR taema-learning (7)
